From 4a76333b368b21c6d2a7bfc6191f0f77352af7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:28:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] sepolicy: restore perf_event in cap2 for huawei 4.14
 kernels

huawei kirin 4.14 kernels backport CAP_PERF_EVENT (38) and list it as
perf_event in the selinux capability2 classmap. their 29.0 vendor
policy grants and neverallows it, but the platform cap2 common only
knows perfmon, so libsepol drops those rules with "failed to resolve
permission perf_event" and hwsched loses the capability.

declare perf_event in cap2 so the vendor rules resolve. kernels that
do not define it ignore the permission.
---
 private/access_vectors | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/private/access_vectors b/private/access_vectors
index 0ffb7ec..2d14f07 100644
--- a/private/access_vectors
+++ b/private/access_vectors
@@ -141,6 +141,7 @@ common cap2
 	perfmon
 	checkpoint_restore
 	bpf
+	perf_event	# CAP_PERF_EVENT (38) on huawei 4.14 kernels
 }
 
 #
